wc3-server

This repository is open-source glue (docker-compose, configuration templates,
Dockerfiles, entrypoints, and docs) that composes third-party open-source
software. The glue is licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE). The software
it builds carries its own licenses:

- PvPGN-PRO (the Battle.net realm) is licensed under the GNU General Public
  License v2.0. This repo builds it from a modified fork,
  github.com/PjSalty/pvpgn-pro-hardened (build hardening plus fixes to the
  packet and tag parsers); that modified source is published there under the
  same license. The container image this repo publishes therefore contains a
  compiled, modified PvPGN, and the corresponding source is the fork.
- The wc3-relay and wc3-mapd daemons are built here from cmd/wc3-relay and
  cmd/wc3-mapd (Go source shared with the wc3-launcher client) under their own
  license.

No Blizzard Entertainment software, binaries, or game data are distributed by
this repository. Warcraft III and Battle.net are trademarks of Blizzard
Entertainment, Inc. You must own Warcraft III; the open-source W3L loader lets a
classic client connect to a non-Blizzard realm, and the game client itself is
never redistributed here.
